title: 'Consequence: a switch that shows the original raw where an overrider stood gives the original a new viewnode ID.'
pid: 691253d1-1e7f-4cf2-89af-aa4e6e872152
body: |2-
  A switch to any perspective, the user's or a foreign owner's, that
  puts an overrider where the original stood raw, or another overrider
  where one stood (A for M becoming U or B), re-points the occurrence in
  place, so its viewnode ID, and the cursor on it, survive. A switch
  that shows the original raw where an overrider stood (back to the root
  authors', or to an owner with no overrider of it) takes the path an
  override's removal takes ('stop_substituting'): the original is
  reinstated beside the overrider, which, no longer warranted, vanishes;
  so the cursor on it moves to the nearest headline. A root is always
  re-pointed, so it keeps its ID every way; its containers folder does
  not ("a replaced root shows its own containers folder", above).
